DATA: the MIT licence above covers the CODE ONLY.

The datasets this repository downloads and the derived files it writes carry their own
terms, and two of them are share-alike. Read this before redistributing any derived layer.

  Ward boundary polygons - DataMeet Municipal_Spatial_Data
    CC BY-SA 2.5 IN, per city. NOTE: the repository's root README states CC BY 4.0, but
    the per-city licence files say CC BY-SA 2.5 IN. The stricter, more specific per-city
    terms are the ones that apply. SHARE-ALIKE: a derived boundary layer you redistribute
    must carry the same licence. data/final/wards.gpkg is such a derived layer.

  Drainage line-work - OpenStreetMap contributors
    ODbL 1.0. SHARE-ALIKE for derived databases. Attribution required.
    data/interim/ward_drain_network.parquet is a derived database.

  BBMP work orders - opencity.in / BBMP
    Public municipal disclosure republished by the Open City Urban Data Portal.

  Ward boundaries (Surat, Bengaluru-GBA) - bharatlas
    Public R2 bucket. Both files checked ship with lat/lon transposed; the pipeline
    corrects this on read and does not redistribute the raw files.

  Copernicus DEM GLO-30 - ESA / Copernicus Programme
    Free and open, attribution required: "produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 (c) DLR
    e.V. 2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under
    COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved."

  CHIRPS - Climate Hazards Center, UC Santa Barbara
    Public domain. Cite Funk et al. (2015), Scientific Data 2:150066.

  CCKP climate indicators - World Bank Climate Change Knowledge Portal
    CC BY 4.0.

  WSF2019 / WSF-Evolution - German Aerospace Center (DLR)
    CC BY 4.0.

  2011 Census attributes - Office of the Registrar General & Census Commissioner, India
    Government of India open data.
